{"key": "56905e60d65a2c986a85604bb734ac49", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "response": {"content": [{"text": "Here are the steps from the sources to restore the connection. They don't give a general restart procedure for a terminal with no connection.\n\n- **Check the chip:** Turn the terminal off and open the back cover. Insert the chip in the slot marked SIM1 or SIM2, metal side facing down. Close the cover, turn it on and wait for the data network to connect. When it shows a connected network (2G or 3G), the terminal is ready to use. Then run a communication test [1].\n- **Turn it off and on:** The method depends on your model. On some, press the green key to turn on and the \".\" key plus the yellow key together for 2 seconds to turn off. On others, press the green key for 5 seconds to turn on and the red key for 5 seconds to turn off. Plug-in models turn on when plugged in and off when unplugged [2].\n- **Signal fluctuation (error ADQ 1-84):** Press the Function key and enter 25. Enter the Operator Password, then select Function 46, and make a test sale. The screen turns green after each step to confirm it [3].\n- **Chip registration error (ADQ 1-87):** Confirm the chip is seated. Press Function, enter 25, enter the Merchant Password, then select Function 46 and then Function 90. Make a test sale [4].\n\nI can propose opening a support ticket for terminal T1988B with the reason \"no connection\". Nothing runs until you confirm, and the proposal expires after 15 minutes [policy:capabilities]. Would you like me to propose it?\n\nMISSING: model-specific restart steps for terminal T1988B", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011Cgk1sHWKx6YfNq3BQ2JsD", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 2887}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2887, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2946, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4, "output_tokens": 513, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}, "role": "agent", "scope": "approval-04#0"}
{"key": "ff27738e860e85ac36427d18eeb5e80f", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "response": {"content": [{"text": "Para uma maquininha com chip sem sinal, o passo a passo do manual de conexão é este:\n\n- Com a máquina desligada, abra a tampa na parte de trás. [1]\n- Insira o chip no local indicado (SIM1 ou SIM2), com a parte metálica voltada para baixo. [1]\n- Feche a tampa, ligue a máquina e aguarde a conexão de rede de dados. [1]\n- Quando aparecer a indicação de rede conectada (2G ou 3G), a máquina está pronta para uso. [1]\n- Faça um teste de comunicação para verificar a conectividade do chip. [1]\n\nSe aparecer o erro ADQ 1-87 (problema no registro do chip) na transação, confirme se o chip está bem inserido. Depois siga a sequência de funções do guia desse erro: tecla de Função, 25, Senha do Lojista, Função 46 e Função 90, e então faça uma venda teste. [5]\n\nSobre o chamado técnico: posso propô-lo para a sua maquininha, com o motivo \"sem sinal\". Ele só é aberto depois da sua confirmação, e a proposta não confirmada expira em 15 minutos. [policy:capabilities] Você confirma a abertura?\n\nOs trechos não trazem o passo a passo do teste de comunicação em si.\n\nMISSING: passos do teste de comunicação do chip", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011Cgk1sNzF931WHn7WYrx3k", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 3002}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3002, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2947, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4, "output_tokens": 470, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}, "role": "agent", "scope": "approval-03#0"}
{"key": "274f29a038a8ae5d7b2e95f93bcd3485", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "response": {"content": [{"text": "Para a maquininha sem sinal conectada por chip, o passo a passo do manual é:\n\n1. Com a máquina desligada, abra a tampa traseira e insira o chip no local sinalizado com SIM1 ou SIM2, com a parte metálica voltada para baixo [1].\n2. Feche a tampa, ligue a máquina e aguarde a conexão de rede de dados [1].\n3. Com a indicação de rede conectada (2G ou 3G), a máquina está pronta para uso [1].\n4. Faça o teste de comunicação: pressione o botão função (F, # ou o da sua máquina), selecione a opção 2 (manutenção) e depois a opção 1 (teste de comunicação) [1][6].\n\nSe o aparelho estiver desligado, as teclas para ligar variam conforme o modelo [4].\n\nQuanto ao chamado técnico, a abertura está **proposta, aguardando sua confirmação**, com o motivo \"sem sinal\" [policy:capabilities]. Nada é executado antes de você confirmar, e a proposta expira em 15 minutos [policy:capabilities].\n\nOs trechos não trazem as teclas de ligar de cada modelo, nem indicam qual delas corresponde à T1988B.\n\nMISSING: teclas de ligar específicas do modelo T1988B", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011Cgk1stdC9rQe6PbDUqX4m", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2559, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4163, "output_tokens": 444, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}, "role": "agent", "scope": "approval-03#0"}
{"key": "c4dcf1abe918d703bb5f539e8a71b1d9", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "response": {"content": [{"text": "The support ticket for terminal T1988B (reason \"no connection\") is drafted but **not opened yet**. Please confirm it (action A-0fa67b1e). The proposal expires after 15 minutes [policy:capabilities].\n\nThe terminal is offline. It connects by chip, shows \"no signal\", and has been offline for 5 hours. Its last contact was 05/11/2026 at 07:26.\n\nYou can try these steps before or while you wait:\n- **Check the chip:** Turn the terminal off and open the back cover. Insert the chip in slot SIM1 or SIM2 with the metal side down. Close the cover and turn it on. Wait for a connected network (2G or 3G), then run a communication test [sup-duvidas-05].\n- **Turn it off and on:** The method depends on the model. Some models use the green key to turn on and the \".\" key plus the yellow key for 2 seconds to turn off. Others use the green key for 5 seconds to turn on and the red key for 5 seconds to turn off. Plug-in models turn on when plugged in and off when unplugged [sup-operacional-01].\n- **If error ADQ 1-84 (signal fluctuation) appears:** Press Function and enter 25. Enter the Operator Password, select Function 46, and make a test sale [sup-erro-adq-1-84-01].\n- **If error ADQ 1-87 (chip registration) appears:** Confirm the chip is seated. Press Function, enter 25, enter the Merchant Password, select Function 46 and then Function 90. Make a test sale [sup-erro-adq-1-87-01].\n\nThe sources don't give restart steps specific to your terminal's model. I can hand this to a human agent if you want.\n\nDo you confirm opening the ticket?", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011Cgk1t2kbuT3uprc61ZNXN", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 939}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 939, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4047, "inference_geo": "